<title>USA: Rockford Industries Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Rockford Industries Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockford Industries Inc</p>
<p>			 (In Thousands, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended March 31 (unaudited)</p>
<p>				1997	     1996,	  1996</p>
<p>						 pro forma</p>
<p>    Shr		   $0.19	    $0.15	   $0.15</p>
<p>    Net		     840		659	     659</p>
<p>    Revenue	     4,596	    3,241	  22,567</p>
<p>    Shrs outstanding  4,380	    4,438	   4,438</p>
<p>NOTES: Rockford said Q1 was best in company's 12-year history. Finance contract originations rose 31 percent to $38.9 million from $29.7 million a year ago. Q1 revenues down $18 million due to adoption of SFAS 125 on Jan. 1. On a pro forma basis, revenues were $4.6 million compared to $3.2 million a year ago, a rise of 42 percent. Rockford finances equipment purchases for the healthcare industry.</p>
</text>
